## Payloads: What the Spell Does

Payloads define the effects applied when hitting the target. A spell can have multiple payloads using `DynamicBuffer`.

### Payload Structure

```csharp
public enum PayloadType : byte
{
    Damage,
    Heal,
    ApplyStatus,
    SpawnEntity
}

public enum ElementalType : byte
{
    Physical,
    Fire,
    Frost,
    Shock,
    Holy
}

public enum StatusEffectType : byte
{
    None,
    Burn,
    Slow,
    Stun,
    Poison
}

public struct PayloadElement : IBufferElementData
{
    public PayloadType Type;
    public ElementalType Element;
    public StatusEffectType Effect;
    public float Amount;
    public float Duration;
}
```

### Example: Multiple Payloads

**JSON**:

```json
{
    "payloads": [
        {
            "type": "damage",
            "amount": 10.0,
            "elemental_type": "fire"
        },
        {
            "type": "apply_status_effect",
            "effect_name": "burn",
            "duration": 5.0
        }
    ]
}
```

**Baking**:

```csharp
// In SpellBakingSystem
var payloadBuffer = ecb.AddBuffer<PayloadElement>(spellEntity);

payloadBuffer.Add(new PayloadElement
{
    Type = PayloadType.Damage,
    Element = ElementalType.Fire,
    Amount = 10f
});

payloadBuffer.Add(new PayloadElement
{
    Type = PayloadType.ApplyStatus,
    Effect = StatusEffectType.Burn,
    Duration = 5f
});
```

### Payload Resolution System

```csharp
[BurstCompile]
[UpdateAfter(typeof(CollisionSystem))]
public partial struct PayloadResolutionSystem : ISystem
{
    [BurstCompile]
    public void OnUpdate(ref SystemState state)
    {
        var ecb = new EntityCommandBuffer(Allocator.TempJob);

        // Process collisions
        foreach (var (payloadBuffer, entity) in
                 SystemAPI.Query<DynamicBuffer<PayloadElement>>()
                         .WithAll<CollisionEvent>()
                         .WithEntityAccess())
        {
            Entity target = GetCollisionTarget(entity);

            // Apply each payload
            foreach (var payload in payloadBuffer)
            {
                switch (payload.Type)
                {
                    case PayloadType.Damage:
                        ApplyDamage(target, payload.Amount, payload.Element);
                        break;

                    case PayloadType.Heal:
                        ApplyHeal(target, payload.Amount);
                        break;

                    case PayloadType.ApplyStatus:
                        ApplyStatusEffect(ecb, target, payload.Effect, payload.Duration);
                        break;

                    case PayloadType.SpawnEntity:
                        SpawnEntity(ecb, GetPosition(entity), payload);
                        break;
                }
            }
        }

        ecb.Playback(state.EntityManager);
        ecb.Dispose();
    }
}
```

## Quick Reference Table

| Category      | JSON Type           | ECS Components                        | Systems                               |
| ------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |
| **Generator** | projectile          | ProjectileTag, Velocity, Lifetime     | MovementSystem, LifetimeSystem        |
| **Generator** | area_of_effect      | AreaOfEffectTag, Radius, Lifetime     | AreaQuerySystem, LifetimeSystem       |
| **Generator** | cone                | ConeTag, Radius, ConeAngle, Direction | ConeQuerySystem, LifetimeSystem       |
| **Modifier**  | homing              | HomingModifier                        | HomingSystem, TargetAcquisitionSystem |
| **Modifier**  | chain               | ChainModifier                         | ChainingSystem                        |
| **Modifier**  | pierce              | PierceModifier                        | CollisionSystem (integrated)          |
| **Modifier**  | fork                | ForkModifier                          | ForkSystem                            |
| **Payload**   | damage              | DynamicBuffer<PayloadElement>         | PayloadResolutionSystem               |
| **Payload**   | heal                | DynamicBuffer<PayloadElement>         | PayloadResolutionSystem               |
| **Payload**   | apply_status_effect | DynamicBuffer<PayloadElement>         | PayloadResolutionSystem               |

## Important Notes

-   The Generator/Modifier/Payload model must be followed strictly
-   **One generator** per spell (mandatory)
-   **Zero or more modifiers** per spell (optional)
-   **One or more payloads** per spell (mandatory)
-   Use **DynamicBuffer<PayloadElement>** for multiple payloads
-   Modifiers are **additive and independent** - can be combined freely
-   Each component should be **small and focused** (Single Responsibility)
-   Systems should be **reusable** - don't couple spell-specific logic
-   Use **tags** for efficient queries (ProjectileTag, AreaOfEffectTag, etc.)
-   Always define **execution order** for systems with dependencies
-   New generators/modifiers/payloads can be added without modifying existing code
